    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d964">

                <pb facs="1018" n="1006" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg1006"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/427: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-26T20:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1941—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1000. Your 1545, August 20, 6 p.m.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d964-f1"/> As a
                    signatory of the Prisoners of War Convention of 1929, not 1939,<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d964-f2"/> and because of its humanitarian interest in the treatment
                    accorded prisoners of war, Department is interested to learn whether the Soviet
                    Government intends to observe this convention. If the Soviet Government does not
                    intend to observe the 1929 but rather an earlier convention the Department would
                    be equally interested to learn of that fact. The Department would assume, of
                    course, that the observation of any such convention by the Soviet Government
                    would be on a reciprocal basis as indicated in the final paragraph of your
                    1458.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d964-f1" n="50" xml:id="d964-f1-content">
